{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","title":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":504,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","line":953,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[Radial equation for distance functions]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0115}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation, thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation, prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.2.10}\n  For a distance function $r:O\\to\\mathbb R$, $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}\\partial_r=0$ and\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial_r}$, where $R_{\\partial_r}(X)=R(X,\\partial_r)\\partial_r$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function}\n\n  \\sketch\n  Because $|\\nabla r|=1$, \\cref{prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation} gives\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}\\partial_r=0$. Substitute $f=r$ in the radial curvature\n  equation; the term involving $S(\\partial_r)$ vanishes, leaving\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial_r}$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[Radial equation for distance functions] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368332d72616469616c2d6571756174696f6e2d64697374616e63652d66756e6374696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0115</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-distance-function-notation\">↗ def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23thm%3Apet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation\">↗ thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation\">↗ prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.2.10</span></span>For a distance function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r:O\\to \\mathbb R$\">$r:O\\to \\mathbb R$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}\\partial _r=0$\">$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}\\partial _r=0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial _r}$\">$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial _r}$</span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R_{\\partial _r}(X)=R(X,\\partial _r)\\partial _r$\">$R_{\\partial _r}(X)=R(X,\\partial _r)\\partial _r$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23cor%3Apet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function\">↗ cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function</a> </p><p>\\sketch Because <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\nabla r|=1$\">$|\\nabla r|=1$</span>, <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368332d6e6f726d616c2d6865737369616e2d72656c6174696f6e\">subsection 2.1</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}\\partial _r=0$\">$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}\\partial _r=0$</span>. Substitute <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f=r$\">$f=r$</span> in the radial curvature equation; the term involving <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S(\\partial _r)$\">$S(\\partial _r)$</span> vanishes, leaving <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial _r}$\">$\\nabla _{\\partial _r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial _r}$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-intrinsic-extrinsic","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-distance-function-curvature-equations","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation","title":"def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation","label":"def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation","label":"thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation","label":"prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","title":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","label":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","title":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","label":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-distance-function-curvature-equations","title":"prop:pet-ch3-distance-function-curvature-equations","label":"prop:pet-ch3-distance-function-curvature-equations"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-jacobi-second-order-equation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-jacobi-second-order-equation","label":"prop:pet-ch3-jacobi-second-order-equation"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","title":"cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[Radial equation for distance functions]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0115}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation, thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation, prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.2.10}\n  For a distance function $r:O\\to\\mathbb R$, $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}\\partial_r=0$ and\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial_r}$, where $R_{\\partial_r}(X)=R(X,\\partial_r)\\partial_r$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch3-radial-equation-distance-function}\n\n  \\sketch\n  Because $|\\nabla r|=1$, \\cref{prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation} gives\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}\\partial_r=0$. Substitute $f=r$ in the radial curvature\n  equation; the term involving $S(\\partial_r)$ vanishes, leaving\n  $\\nabla_{\\partial_r}S+S^2=-R_{\\partial_r}$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation","title":"def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-radial-curvature-equation","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-normal-hessian-relation","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}